3,"Quichua Chimborazo language. Evangelism tools, church planting resources, Christian songs and audio bible study materials. Download free MP3s.",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/qug,"Each program is a customised and culturally relevant selection of scripts, and may include songs and music. ... Jesus Film Project films - Quichua, Highland, Chimborazo - (Jesus Film Project) The New Testament - Quichua, Chimborazo Highland - (Faith Comes By Hearing) Central Highland Quichua Chaupi Urcucuna Kichwa Chimborazo Chimborazo Highland Quichua Chimborazo Quichua Ecuadorean Quechua Ecuadorian Quecha Highland Ecuadorian Quichua Kichwa Kichwa de la Sierra Kichwa Shimi Quechua: Ecuadorean Quichua, Chimborazo Highland (ISO Language Name) Quichua de Chimborazo Quichua de la Sierra Quichua de la Sierra Chimborazo Quichua: Highland: Chimborazo Quichua Serrano Central Runa Shimi Quichua del Chimborazo","Quichua, Chimborazo Highland",Quechuan
4,"LIVE - Quechua - Kabra ŃAWY - Quena - Native Music ...Quechua music - YouTubeQuichua, Chimborazo Highland - worldmission.mediaQuichua Chimborazo language. Evangelism tools, church ...Quichua, Chimborazo Highland Language (QUG) – L1 & L2 ...Quichua Instruments - incasite.com",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eJsjkZsLZEs,"Please subscribe to receive more music directly from Wuauquikuna. Visit our website wuauquikuna-official.com Wuauquikuna performs at the festivals, concerts, events and other venues throughout... Traditional music from the Andes: Chasca - Carullaktama Sebastian Ursich 122K views • 16 years ago 2 Interesting point: The Quichua language is intertwined with traditional Andean music and poetry, often used in ritualistic and communal events. Audio recordings available in Quichua Chimborazo These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who are not literate or are from oral cultures, particularly unreached people groups. It belongs to the Quechuan language family and is part of the Quechua macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. A significant part of their culture is their music. It is considered to have a spiritual capacity and many of the melodies and rhythms are intended to represent the different aspects of their lives and their relationship to mother earth, or ""Pacha Mama"".","Quichua, Chimborazo Highland",Quechuan
